INSERT INTO test_step (id, step_name, step_description, expected_result, script_id, created_date, updated_at) VALUES ('455ed7aa-652f-479b-bfe6-bdc6630dd92e', 'STEP 1', '1)Load the module
2)Get the  Manageable Notification status using Device.DeviceInfo.X_RDKCENTRAL-COM_RFC.Feature.ManageableNotification.Enable Check if enabled  if not enable it.
3)Check for PARODUSlog.txt.0 and Consolelog.txt.0 file presence.
4)Capture the tail -f of /rdklogs/logs/PARODUSlog.txt.0 in /nvram/tdk_PARODUStail
5)Capture the tail -f of /rdklogs/logs/Consolelog.txt.0 in /nvram/tdk_Consoletail
6)Trigger a reboot via Webpa  using Device.X_CISCO_COM_DeviceControl.RebootDevice set  to "Device"
7)Grep for the following in tdk_PAMtail
grep -i "reboot-pending" /nvram/tdk_PARODUStail
grep -i "PARODUS: SIGTERM received" /nvram/tdk_PARODUStail
grep -i "PARODUS: cloud_status set as offline after connection close" /nvram/tdk_PARODUStail
grep -i "PARODUS: SIGTERM received" /nvram/tdk_PARODUStail
grep -i "Shutdown parodus" /nvram/tdk_Consoletail
8) Remove the file created rm -rf /nvram/tdk_PARODUStail and /nvram/tdk_Consoletail
9)Revert the Manageable Notification status to default if set
10)Unload the Module', 'The log Message "reboot-pending","PARODUS: SIGTERM received","PARODUS: cloud_status set as offline after connection close","PARODUS: SIGTERM received","Shutdown parodus", should be available in the logs captured at the time of reboot initiation', '8ddca78e-c32c-4209-8e40-e9efa5dc3e4d', '2026-07-24 09:22:10.235159', '2026-07-24 09:22:10.235160');
DELETE FROM test_step WHERE script_id = '2949ff9b-f963-49e2-af8a-5f4b23ad229a';
INSERT INTO test_step (id, step_name, step_description, expected_result, script_id, created_date, updated_at) VALUES ('4671753e-67be-416f-8bdd-2a5593f46601', 'STEP 1', '1. Load tdkb_e2e module
2. Using tdkb_e2e_Get, get and save LanIP,SubnetMask,Maximum and minimum Address range
3. Set LanIP,SubnetMask,Maximum and minimum Address range as ClassA using tdkb_e2e_SetMultipleParams
4. Set subnetmask to multicast IP using tdkb_e2e_SetMultipleParams and it should fail
5.  Connect to the LAN client and check whether the subnetmask changed or not
5. Revert the values to original value
6.Unload tdkb_e2e module', 'DHCP configuration on client should not be affected by setting subnetmask as multicast IP', '2949ff9b-f963-49e2-af8a-5f4b23ad229a', '2026-07-30 05:18:08.436521', '2026-07-30 05:18:08.436522');
DELETE FROM test_step WHERE script_id = 'eaa5cf08-4e2c-44dd-b05c-81db2053dc8b';
INSERT INTO test_step (id, step_name, step_description, expected_result, script_id, created_date, updated_at) VALUES ('46fbc657-c946-4b29-bdd8-c1fa7d617468', 'STEP 1', '1. Load tdkb_e2e module
2. Using tdkb_e2e_Get, get and save LanIP,SubnetMask,Maximum and minimum Address range
3. Set LanIP,SubnetMask,Maximum and minimum Address range as ClassB using tdkb_e2e_SetMultipleParams
4.  Connect to the LAN  client and check whether the IP obtained is in valid range
5. Revert the values to original value
6.Unload tdkb_e2e module', 'The IP obtained by the lan client should be in Class B private range', 'eaa5cf08-4e2c-44dd-b05c-81db2053dc8b', '2026-07-29 11:33:36.061511', '2026-07-29 11:33:36.061513');
DELETE FROM test_step WHERE script_id = '98f2319f-bf74-4681-a3aa-d98c64de5c97';
INSERT INTO test_step (id, step_name, step_description, expected_result, script_id, created_date, updated_at) VALUES ('4770ae3b-61a2-4dfa-b92f-1bcb357f4ec7', 'STEP 1', '1.Initiate SSH connection to execute command remotely.
2.Retrieve the NATIVE_PLAYBACK_CHECK_AV_STATUS and NATIVE_PLAYBACK_MEDIAPLAYBACK_TIMEOUT config values from Device config file.
3.Retrieve the video_src_url_hls variable from MediaValidationVariables library
4.Construct the mediapipelinetests command based on the retrieved video url, testcasename, NATIVE_PLAYBACK_CHECK_AV_STATUS deviceconfig value and timeout
5.Execute the command in DUT. During the execution, the DUT will playback av for NATIVE_PLAYBACK_MEDIAPLAYBACK_TIMEOUT seconds then application exits by closing the pipeline
6.Verify the output from the execute command and check if the strings "Failures: 0" and "Errors: 0", or "failed: 0" exists in the returned output
7.Based on the ExecuteCommand() return value and the output returned from the mediapipelinetests application, TM return SUCCESS/FAILURE status.
8.Verify duration is matched with the expected duration', '1. Verify the API call is success
Checkpoint 2. Verify that the output returned from mediapipelinetests contains the strings "Failures: 0" and "Errors: 0", or "failed: 0"
Checkpoint 3. Verify that duration is retrieved as expected', '98f2319f-bf74-4681-a3aa-d98c64de5c97', '2026-07-16 09:32:37.348385', '2026-07-16 09:32:37.348386');
DELETE FROM test_step WHERE script_id = 'acfc7038-473d-4565-80e1-06517142ee32';
