INSERT INTO test_step (id, step_name, step_description, expected_result, script_id, created_date, updated_at) VALUES ('ad96afa9-24e1-4103-98b0-467d7bb56598', 'STEP 1', '1. Load the E2E, Advanced Config Modules
2. Check if Device.NAT.X_CISCO_COM_PortTriggers.Enable is enabled, if not enable it.
3. Get the current SSID, KeyPassphrase and radio enable of 2G radio.
4. Set current SSID, KeyPassphrase to new values as per the config file and radio enable to true.
5. Connect the WLAN client to the WiFi SSID and retrieve its IP address corresponding interface name configured.
6. Check if the wlan IP is in the expected DHCP range.
7. Add a new instance to the port triggering rule table
8. To the added instance, configure the rule: Trigger Port(start:end) - 1234:1244, TargetPort(start:end) - 5001:5001 (for IPERF), Trigger Protocol - UDP, Target Protocol - UDP, Description - MyPTRule
9. Enable the added port trigger rule
10. Check if the rule is added and enabled successfully by fetching the values of corresponding DMs
11. Add a static route in the WLAN client so that an outbound packet can be sent from the client via the DUT GW to the external network
12. Send an outbound packet to trigger a randomly chosen port in range 1234:1244 with a UDP packet
13. From WAN client, send an inbound packet to the target port 5001 via the DUT GW WAN IP. The packet should be successfully forwarded to the WLAN client.
14. Delete the added route
15. Delete the added port triggering rule
16. Revert SSID, Keypassphrase and radio enable to initial values
17. Revert Device.NAT.X_CISCO_COM_PortTriggers.Enable if required
18. Unload the modules', 'Port Triggering rule should take effect when the trigger port is between the range (triggerPortStart, triggerPortEnd) and the target port is 5001 (IPERF).', 'fd3563f2-ab62-4c8b-95f7-71c0abcdd208', '2026-07-30 08:33:53.234676', '2026-07-30 08:33:53.234677');
DELETE FROM test_step WHERE script_id = 'b35c85b3-1f66-42fc-8ef5-f6b9e3d5e767';
INSERT INTO test_step (id, step_name, step_description, expected_result, script_id, created_date, updated_at) VALUES ('adc2a309-19b6-4366-916d-8f0fb91ab082', 'STEP 1', '1.Configure the Function info in Test Manager GUI  which needs to be tested
(AdvancedConfig_Set, AdvancedConfig_AddObject - func name - "If not exists already"
 advancedconfig - module name
 Necessary I/P args as Mentioned in Input)
2.Python Script will be generated/overrided automically by Test Manager with provided arguments in configure page (TS_ADVANCEDCONFIG_PTDuplicateServiceName.py)
3.Execute the generated Script(TS_ADVANCEDCONFIG_PTDuplicateServiceName.py) using execution page of  Test Manager GUI
4.advancedconfigstub which is a part of TDK Agent process, will be in listening mode to execute TDK Component function named AdvancedConfig_Set,AdvancedConfig_AddObject through registered TDK advancedconfigstub function along with necessary Entry Values as arguments
5.AdvancedConfig_Set function will call ssp_setParameterValue,that inturn will call CCSP Base Interface Function named CcspBaseIf_setParameterValues.
6. AdvancedConfig_AddObject function will call ssp_addTableRow, that inturn will call CCSP Base Interface Function named CcspBaseIf_AddTblRow and AdvancedConfig_GetNames Will find the instance number of the row added and will process the function for the instance number generated.
7.Responses(printf) from TDK Component,Ccsp Library function and advancedcongifstub would be logged in Agent Console log based on the debug info redirected to agent console
8.advancedconfigstub will validate the available result (from ssp_setParameterValue as zero) with expected result (zero) and the result is updated in agent console log and json output variable
9.TestManager will publish the result in GUI as SUCCESS/FAILURE based on the response from AdvancedConfig_Set and AdvancedConfig_AddObject functions.', 'Checkpoint 1:
Check if Advanced -> Port Triggering -> Service name option for port Triggering rule functionality works.
CheckPoint 2:
Success log should be available in Agent Console Log
CheckPoint 3:
TDK agent Test Function will log the test case result as SUCCESS based on API response
CheckPoint 4:
TestManager GUI will publish the result as SUCCESS in Execution page', 'b35c85b3-1f66-42fc-8ef5-f6b9e3d5e767', '2026-07-29 10:31:41.400650', '2026-07-29 10:31:41.400652');
DELETE FROM test_step WHERE script_id = '1db3c21b-551f-4adc-8f69-0cbabe785068';
INSERT INTO test_step (id, step_name, step_description, expected_result, script_id, created_date, updated_at) VALUES ('ae055036-b236-4ba2-aaad-08a2c00608dd', 'STEP 1', '1. Load tdkb_e2e module
2. Using tdkb_e2e_Get, get and save firewall level
3. Set the firewall level to Low using tdkb_e2e_SetMultipleParams
4. Connect to Wifi client to GW SSID and check whether it is assigned a valid ip by the GW
5. From the wlan client, do PING to the WAN client and check whether PING is success when the firewall level is set to High
6. Revert the firewall level to original value
7.Unload tdkb_e2e module', 'PING from WLAN to WAN should pass through', '1db3c21b-551f-4adc-8f69-0cbabe785068', '2026-07-29 10:43:17.337898', '2026-07-29 10:43:17.337899');
